  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit, Bash, Skill(code-review)</tools>
  <outputs>SummarizeFilesWizard on WizardFollowOns; duplicates deleted; project-wide duplicate-free confirmation.</outputs>

  <completion-notes>
    <summary>
      SummarizeFilesWizard migrated onto the shared, config-driven WizardFollowOns
      module. The local Next-Steps grid + Send Email step (562 LOC across two
      files) were deleted and replaced by a FollowOnCardConfig[] consumed by the
      shared FollowOnGrid + SendEmailFollowOnStep. Net −531 lines in the folder.
      TypeScript typecheck clean (whole lib), eslint clean, WizardFollowOns +
      related tests pass (7/7). code-review = APPROVE (0 critical/0 warning),
      adr-check = 0 violations.
    </summary>
    <files-changed>
      MODIFIED src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SummarizeFilesWizard/SummarizeFilesDialog.tsx
      MODIFIED src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SummarizeFilesWizard/index.ts
      DELETED  src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SummarizeFilesWizard/SummaryNextStepsStep.tsx
      DELETED  src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SummarizeFilesWizard/SummarizeSendEmailStep.tsx
    </files-changed>
    <how-renderSelectedExtra-was-used>
      The "include only short summary in email" toggle that the old
      SummaryNextStepsStep rendered inline in the grid (only while Send Email is
      selected) is now expressed as the send-email card's `renderSelectedExtra`
      slot — exactly the case the slot was added for. No grid fork. The Send
      Email dynamic step also keeps its own copy of the toggle via
      SendEmailFollowOnStep's `headerContent` slot (matching the original, which
      showed the toggle in both places). Both are wired to the same
      includeShortSummary state/ref.
    </how-renderSelectedExtra-was-used>
    <design-decisions>
      - Card set preserved verbatim: send-email / create-project / work-on-analysis
        (the last two are intentionally non-canonical plain-string ids — expected
        per design §5.9 / followOnTypes doc). Labels, descriptions, icons
        (Mail/FolderAdd/ClipboardTask @28px) and canonical order unchanged.
      - Removed the imperative prev/next diff useEffect + handleSkipAction +
        prevSelectedActionsRef; FollowOnGrid now injects/removes each dynamic step
        at click time via shellRef. Step bodies read dialog form state via refs
        (same stale-closure-proof pattern as before).
      - Relocated buildSummaryEmailSubject/buildSummaryEmailBody + the
        SummaryActionId union into SummarizeFilesDialog.tsx (were exported from
        the deleted SummarizeSendEmailStep); index.ts re-points there, so the
        public API is unchanged. No external consumer (pcf/solutions) imported the
        deleted symbols — verified by grep.
      - Did NOT touch src/components/index.ts (task 021 owns it) — the root barrel
        does `export * from './SummarizeFilesWizard'`, so dropping the deleted
        symbols from the local barrel is sufficient and non-conflicting.
    </design-decisions>
    <behavioral-delta>
      One intentional change: the old Skip was a custom footer button that
      DESELECTED the card (removing its sidebar step). The shared model uses
      IWizardStepConfig.isSkippable, whose Skip ADVANCES without deselecting.
      Mitigation: handleFinish's create-project branch now additionally guards on
      projectFormValidRef.current, so a skipped/invalid Create Project can no
      longer fire createProject(EMPTY_PROJECT_FORM). This preserves the original
      invariant (the old flow could never Finish with an invalid create-project
      step selected, since Finish was canAdvance-gated). send-email already
      self-guards on emailTo.trim(); work-on-analysis is side-effect-free. Guard +
      rationale documented inline.
    </behavioral-delta>
    <regression>
      No SummarizeFilesDialog unit-test harness exists; the follow-on mechanics
      are covered by the shared FollowOnGrid.test.tsx (select→addDynamicStep with
      derived id + canonical order, per-card stepLabel/isSkippable/canAdvance,
      deselect→removeDynamicStep, renderSelectedExtra inline toggle) — all pass.
      Card labels/descriptions/icons/order, canAdvance predicates, step ids
      (followon-*), and the email pre-fill + short-summary-rebuild effects were
      verified identical to the deleted originals by direct comparison.
    </regression>
    <own-scope-duplicate-grep>
      Recursive find for *nextstep*/*sendemail*/*followon* files, at check time
      (2026-07-08): SummarizeFilesWizard = CLEAN (0 local follow-on files),
      CreateMatterWizard = CLEAN. Still present (sibling in-flight work, NOT this
      task's concern): CreateRecordWizard/steps/SendEmailStep.tsx (task 021),
      CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/CreateFollowOnEventStep.tsx (task 023). Cannot
      assert full project-wide single-implementation completeness from my own
      scope — tasks 021/023 must land first. My scope's contribution to the
      zero-duplicates criterion is complete.
    </own-scope-duplicate-grep>
    <quality-gates>
      code-review: APPROVE — 0 critical, 0 warning; net −531 LOC (Quality
      Improved); 0 AI code smells. adr-check: 0 violations — ADR-012/021/022
      compliant (no PCF leak, no v8 imports, no hardcoded colors). typecheck +
      eslint clean.
    </quality-gates>
  </completion-notes>

